{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$(date -u +%FT%TZ) [sol] Classification appears ONLY even K, unique symmetric triangle {(h,h,0),(h,0,h),(0,h,h)}, K=2h. Slice impossible: forced full slice x_i=a, but adjacent allocation y_i=a+1 cannot be dominated (strict gains in other two need total >=2 while slice has just 1 extra). Up triangle vertices m+d e_i: all lattice points >=m undominated -> d=1; then any m_i>0 gives opposite witness, so K=1 only. Down triangle vertices m+h(1-e_i): each cap y_j>=m_j+h,y_k>=m_k+h is undominated; if m_i>0 cap has extra point. Thus m=0, K=2h. Working rigorous structural lemma proof now.\" >> /work/board.md; cat /work/board.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
